.</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyle</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Maher</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cairns</surname><given-names>C.J.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lloyd</surname><given-names>S.M.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Elimination of central-venous-catheter-related bloodstream infections from the intensive care unit</article-title><source>BMJ Qual Saf</source><volume>20</volume><issue>2</issue><year>2011</year><fpage>174</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmjqs.2009.037200</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><label>6</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref6"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Battistella</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhola</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lok</surname><given-names>C.E.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Long-term follow-up of the hemodialysis infection prevention with polysporin ointment (HIPPO) Study: a quality improvement report</article-title><source>Am J Kidney Dis</source><volume>57</volume><issue>3</issue><year>2011</year><fpage>432</fpage><lpage>441</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/j.ajkd.2010.10.009</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21216512</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref7"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hammarskj&#x000f6;ld</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanberger</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Taxbro</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Malmvall</surname><given-names>B.-E.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sustained low incidence of central venous catheter-related infections over six years in a Swedish hospital with an active central venous catheter team</article-title><source>Am J Infect Control</source><volume>42</volume><issue>2</issue><year>2014</year><fpage>122</fpage><lpage>128</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ajic.2013.09.023</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">24485369</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref8"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rinke</surname><given-names>M.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Heo</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Saiman</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bundy</surname><given-names>D.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenberg</surname><given-names>R.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>DeLaMora</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Pediatric ambulatory central Line&#x02013;associated bloodstream infections</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source><volume>147</volume><issue>1</issue><year>2021</year><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1542/peds.2020-0524</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref9"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Valik</surname><given-names>J.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanushi</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000fc;llersdorf</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ternhag</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Aufwerber</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Validation of automated sepsis surveillance based on the Sepsis-3 clinical criteria against physician record review in a general hospital population: observational study using electronic health records data</article-title><source>BMJ Qual Saf</source><volume>29</volume><issue>9</issue><year>2020</year><fpage>735</fpage><lpage>745</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmjqs-2019-010123</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref10"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McNamara</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Adams</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dellit</surname><given-names>T.H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improving central venous catheter insertion documentation to facilitate electronic surveillance of bundle compliance</article-title><source>Am J Infect Control</source><volume>39</volume><issue>9</issue><year>2011</year><fpage>779</fpage><lpage>781</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ajic.2010.12.009</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21664723</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref11"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thate</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossetti</surname><given-names>S.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>McDermott-Levy</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Moriarty</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identifying best practices in electronic health record documentation to support interprofessional communication for the prevention of central line-associated bloodstream infections</article-title><source>Am J Infect Control</source><volume>48</volume><issue>2</issue><year>2020</year><fpage>124</fpage><lpage>131</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ajic.2019.07.027</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">31606258</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref12"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bj&#x000f6;rkander</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></